#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050040 :topic/id #uuid "28069d76-f5fe-52d4-9061-6a927a6607e1" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147436 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147353 :question/id #uuid "10aa6257-c3f8-59c6-802e-b4a29fca49ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-6627" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2x^2 y'' + 6 xy' + 2y = 0, \\qquad x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume the solutions take the form $y=x^\\lambda.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny' = \\lambda x^{\\lambda -1}, \\qquad y'' = \\lambda(\\lambda-1)x^{\\lambda-2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+6x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+2{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+6\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+2{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+6\\lambda +2] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+6\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ 2(\\lambda +1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation has a double root $\\lambda = -1.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={c}_{1}{x}^{-1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{1}}{x}+\\frac{{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abe724a-6aec-5c11-8a00-d92e616a06d7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32c35b1d-b053-543d-b551-1716f1b6fb91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333459} {:answer/id #uuid "3fab292e-ca32-5021-bf39-efb360836747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333591} {:answer/id #uuid "88db84b0-c6c6-57b5-8c73-ede872283f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-1}+{c}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334204} {:answer/id #uuid "e7eff46d-ce18-5320-ae7d-ccec6c0588ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}{x}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335012} {:answer/id #uuid "fc41558a-e388-59c7-8849-ec9163a8d3b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fab292e-ca32-5021-bf39-efb360836747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333591} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e561dbb-816f-537f-9d8e-91c1c5702aa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fc350f02-9855-549a-a75a-59038b31fab4" :question/math-academy-id "q-64777" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +1] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =1.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "828d2c05-5bef-5066-b5eb-e07255f21fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t) = c_{1}t^{6} + c_{2}t^{-6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146895} {:answer/id #uuid "9211ec67-966b-5af8-932c-92d1dc2b112d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t) = c_{1}t^{-3} + c_{2}t^{-3}\\ln t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146896} {:answer/id #uuid "afee6923-9321-5270-b4de-12ae29be6782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t) = c_{1}t^{6} + c_{2}t^{6}\\ln t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146897} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e69e4d-f6ab-5631-8024-4d1826c66c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t) = c_{1}t^{3} + c_{2}t^{3}\\ln t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146898} {:answer/id #uuid "e84a6e87-8004-5548-bc6b-b6d302d441e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t) = c_{1}t^{3} + c_{2}\\ln t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4e69e4d-f6ab-5631-8024-4d1826c66c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t) = c_{1}t^{3} + c_{2}t^{3}\\ln t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146898} :answer-field/id #uuid "c38a0d72-2264-5fad-8897-9dd1bc343b56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dadb2653-fa33-5c67-b21a-f4fc2e901bda" :question/math-academy-id "q-64876" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$3t^{2}y^{″} - 15ty^{′} + 27y = 0, t > 0$." :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}-15t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+27{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 3\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }-15\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+27{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[3\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-15\\lambda +27] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-15\\lambda +27 & =0 \\\\ 3{\\lambda }^{2}-18\\lambda +27 & =0 \\\\ 3({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9) & =0 \\\\ 3(\\lambda -3)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =3.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln} t.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0532fb13-38c8-598f-a484-b7ba6880bbe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{6}+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235833} {:answer/id #uuid "3412195b-c26c-5b9e-8c50-6eb4354d8dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-6}+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236149} {:answer/id #uuid "52b71e72-a3d9-594b-a458-21e5ad394c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{6}+{c}_{2}{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236341} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb27694-23e9-5075-a639-98a4cb8e2f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{x}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237123} {:answer/id #uuid "f1dde908-d447-5df0-8cc6-0fef77322f37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-4}+{c}_{2}{x}^{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52b71e72-a3d9-594b-a458-21e5ad394c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{6}+{c}_{2}{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236341} :answer-field/id #uuid "800eac44-90a5-5b5b-849e-917bbfe402f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9372000a-a262-5823-8d55-11add35abca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-102348" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-11x{y}^{′}+36y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-11x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+36{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-11\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+36{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-11\\lambda +36] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-11\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-12\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =6.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{6}+{c}_{2}{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2775d710-02ba-5e75-9671-92874f512265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333350} {:answer/id #uuid "4908566d-0cd5-5be9-91fb-ae9254b720ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333662} {:answer/id #uuid "d9505d59-c070-5f9b-8ad2-86ec138466d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{3}+{c}_{2}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334897} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b6409a-fea9-587b-b2cc-38ad686fa076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334956} {:answer/id #uuid "fb7a99dd-1ccb-5bf7-b28f-fe13d278a381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-3}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4908566d-0cd5-5be9-91fb-ae9254b720ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333662} :answer-field/id #uuid "cabe4145-c1d2-5066-89fa-583e4bca4aeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0d0baceb-8850-5507-a962-183cfbdfc087" :question/math-academy-id "q-64785" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+19x{y}^{′}+81y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+19x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+81{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+19\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+81{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+19\\lambda +81] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+19\\lambda +81 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+18\\lambda +81 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-9.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28387815-0778-5837-8c6d-5d4ad7a54533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333360} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe7fd38-9b39-5304-b580-839933a9d6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333865} {:answer/id #uuid "77d0cbf4-556b-575b-a428-a730f60821f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334064} {:answer/id #uuid "be913b43-c157-51f5-8392-e8632b90d9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-1}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334638} {:answer/id #uuid "c03cc404-5dc8-58b8-b55d-2a3e7c36a1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28387815-0778-5837-8c6d-5d4ad7a54533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333360} :answer-field/id #uuid "81120bdd-fa77-54b5-9824-4a21480d0f83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "223f7f71-6ddd-55f4-b3be-55a320e3046f" :question/math-academy-id "q-64872" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+10t{y}^{′}+8y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+10t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+8{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+10\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+8{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+10\\lambda +8] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+10\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-2.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7b6013-2fc9-5a25-9d4a-33014cc1c1f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333390} {:answer/id #uuid "54563e8f-0ecd-5a77-9950-7e320d87fdb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333757} {:answer/id #uuid "61666995-83cc-5a03-a1ec-29cf03b6f05e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333877} {:answer/id #uuid "6df5183d-1134-5bbd-b43e-9547db1afd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333987} {:answer/id #uuid "84115afe-77e3-5822-bf46-21c0785f2dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a7b6013-2fc9-5a25-9d4a-33014cc1c1f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333390} :answer-field/id #uuid "4764173c-9ecd-5a23-8a49-78424a8dabe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ac369f7a-9688-5ad0-887d-e6746cbb5897" :question/math-academy-id "q-64874" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+22t{y}^{′}+50y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+22t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+50{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+22\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+50{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+22\\lambda +50] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+22\\lambda +50 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+20\\lambda +50 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+10\\lambda +25) & =0 \\\\ 2(\\lambda +5)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-5.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d24b176-040d-52e9-8542-7c6481104c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{4}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333105} {:answer/id #uuid "15bb3fd0-2cf6-5c9d-9359-b1bb04ea9302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333184} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdf1386-5f0a-52c1-8f7b-dfe5db7f2bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333249} {:answer/id #uuid "4f9fb064-74a4-569b-bd45-577b9a7301ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333717} {:answer/id #uuid "acfb920f-8cd8-56ba-a950-7c44b64b6632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{4}+{c}_{2}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f9fb064-74a4-569b-bd45-577b9a7301ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333717} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce3a9137-8892-55d1-8ac9-1ce92b58e97d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2263ded7-e653-5285-b554-051f24c61a10" :question/math-academy-id "q-64875" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+15x{y}^{′}+49y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+15x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+49{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+15\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+49{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+15\\lambda +49] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+15\\lambda +49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+14\\lambda +49 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +7)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-7.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28080de3-c714-52ee-98e9-6a9abc0043cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333357} {:answer/id #uuid "36ea631e-7ff4-5cb2-9643-743e9bb20a99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333494} {:answer/id #uuid "5eba75a9-a1bf-5808-ba90-7be0f1cc1d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333853} {:answer/id #uuid "6433b997-575c-5087-9919-c88f93a4495d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333898} {:answer/id #uuid "680ebcad-0d8a-5f68-97a9-4bcc955441ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5eba75a9-a1bf-5808-ba90-7be0f1cc1d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218633